     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks like an error.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. That is double the usual maximum of 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release metformin (2,000 mg/day for extended-release). A single 1,700 mg dose is also well above the usual maximum of about 1,000 mg per dose. An overdose raises the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity, even with normal renal function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals** (2,550 mg/day, the max dose)\n- **1,700 mg/day total**, for example 850 mg PO twice daily with meals\n- **Another dose**, such as 500 mg or 1,000 mg twice daily\n\nIf you do want 1,700 mg three times daily, tell me and I'll enter it with a note recording that you confirmed the dose. Otherwise, give me the corrected dose and frequency and I'll enter it right away."
      }
     ],
